格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Local-first desktop workspace for ACP agents—DeepSeek Harness, Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Hermes, and OpenClaw—with projects, tools, files, browser, and sessions.","id":"gh:1262601114","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"backchat","slug":"openma-ai/backchat","topics":["acp","agent-client-protocol","ai-agents","claude-code","codex","deepseek-harness","desktop-app","developer-tools","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins","electron","gemini-cli","hermes","local-first","mcp","mcp-apps","multi-agent","opencode","productivity"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Local-first desktop workspace for ACP agents—DeepSeek Harness, Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, OpenC"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ode, Hermes, and OpenClaw—with projects, tools, files, browser, and sessions."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"Backchat"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"A multi-agent desktop for Agent Client Protocol (ACP) harnesses, tools, and outputs."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Visit the official website →"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"New: DeepSeek Harness support through dsh-plugin and dsh-acp."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Use your existing dsh profile or the standalone ACP server from the same desktop."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Backchat gives developer agents a shared desktop without taking away the things\nthat make each harne"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"ss useful. Bring multiple agents into one conversation and\nkeep the built-in browser, files, termina"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"l, MCP Apps, and Codex plugins close."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Why Backchat"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"- **One workspace, many agents.** Run Claude Code, Codex CLI, DeepSeek Harness,\nGemini CLI, OpenCode"},{"id":"p9s2","text":", Hermes, or OpenClaw from the same desktop surface.\n- **Agent-aware, not vendor-shaped.** Backchat "},{"id":"p9s3","text":"surfaces the capabilities,\ncommands, models, modes, and permissions reported by the active harness\ni"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"nstead of inventing a generic capability layer.\n- **Project-scoped context.** Sessions are grouped b"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"y their working directory,\nso files, terminals, browser state, and conversations stay attached to th"},{"id":"p9s6","text":"e\nproject where the work happened.\n- **Projects can span related folders.** One primary folder suppl"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"ies the chat\ncwd, Git context, and project instructions; secondary folders extend the\nagent's file s"},{"id":"p9s8","text":"cope through ACP `additionalDirectories`.\n- **Built-in tools that stay in the flow.** Browse the web"},{"id":"p9s9","text":", inspect files, start\na terminal, attach images, and work without leaving the conversation.\n- **Nat"},{"id":"p9s10","text":"ive extensions and apps.** Render interactive MCP Apps directly in a\nturn and use Codex plugins with"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"out flattening them into generic text output.\n- **Multi-agent conversations.** Bring several harness"},{"id":"p9s12","text":"es into one chat, or use\nside chats, ACP forks, and native subagent activity when available.\n- **Rep"},{"id":"p9s13","text":"eatable work.** Create one-time or recurring schedules that run against a\nproject and harness, with "},{"id":"p9s14","text":"eate one-time or recurring schedules that run against a\nproject and harness, with local run history."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## A few things you can see"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"These snapshots come from the E2E suite (`e2e/readme-screenshots.spec.ts`)."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Each turn folds its work into one readable activity line."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Light and dark themes, with syntax-highlighted file previews."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Pop out a live result when the work needs more room."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Interactive MCP Apps rendered directly in a turn."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Supported agents"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Backchat currently ships registry entries for:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| Agent | ACP entry | Notes |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| Claude Code | `claude-acp` | Claude Code through the official ACP adapter |\n| Codex CLI | `codex-a"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"cp` | Codex through `codex-acp` |\n| Pi | `openma-acp-pi-acp` | Pi through `@openma/pi-acp` |\n| DeepS"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"eek Harness | `dsh-acp` or `dsh --profile acp` | Standalone ACP server or dsh profile plugin |\n| Gem"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"ini CLI | `gemini` | Gemini CLI's ACP mode |\n| OpenCode | `opencode` | OpenCode's ACP mode |\n| Herme"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"s | `hermes` | Hermes ACP entry |\n| OpenClaw | `openclaw` | OpenClaw ACP entry |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness can be connected in either form:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"See openma-ai/deepseek-harness-acp\nfor authentication, profile, model, permission, and MCP configura"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"penma-ai/deepseek-harness-acp\nfor authentication, profile, model, permission, and MCP configuration."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Agent binaries are discovered or configured from **Settings → Agents**. The\nregistry and setup layer"},{"id":"p23s2","text":" are deliberately separate from the chat UI, so adding\nor updating a harness does not require changi"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"ng the conversation model."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"### Run from source"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Requirements: Node.js 24 and pnpm 11.24.0 (matching CI)."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"The shared `@openma/common` dependency is pinned to the immutable Git tag\n`v0.7.3`; no sibling check"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"out or local link is required. The OpenMA SDK and daemon\nconnection snapshots live under `packages/`"},{"id":"p28s3","text":" with their upstream provenance."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"On first launch, open **Settings → Agents** to install or point Backchat at an\nACP-compatible agent,"},{"id":"p29s2","text":" then choose a project and start a chat."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"### Build and package"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Signed release packaging and notarization are documented in\n`docs/releasing.md`."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## Development commands"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"Pull requests run `test:ci` and `test:e2e:fast`. Pushes to `main` also build an\nunsigned macOS DMG, "},{"id":"p35s2","text":"then check that the packaged app can import its runtime and\ncomplete a first prompt. The website dow"},{"id":"p35s3","text":"nload button always points at\nhttps://github.com/openma-ai/backchat/releases/latest/download/Backcha"},{"id":"p35s4","text":"t-arm64.dmg\n; tagged releases upload that stable filename next to the versioned DMG.\nGitHub's offici"},{"id":"p35s5","text":"al Dependency Review, CodeQL, and Dependabot for Actions run\nalongside those gates."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"The desktop shell is built with Electron, TypeScript, React, Vite, Tailwind\nCSS, and shadcn/ui. The "},{"id":"p36s2","text":"ACP runtime is vendored from\n`open-managed-agents` and\ntrimmed to the local desktop use case."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## How the pieces fit together"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"1. **Choose a project.** A project is a working directory and the anchor for\nsessions and local arti"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"facts.\n2. **Choose a harness.** Backchat starts the selected ACP agent as a local\nchild process and "},{"id":"p38s3","text":"keeps its real configuration and capabilities visible.\n3. **Work in one surface.** Conversation even"},{"id":"p38s4","text":"ts, tool activity, MCP Apps,\nfiles, browser tabs, and terminals are projected into the same task.\n4."},{"id":"p38s5","text":" **Branch when useful.** Continue in a side chat, fork an ACP session when\nsupported, or follow nati"},{"id":"p38s6","text":"ve subagent activity emitted by the harness."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"## Status"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"Backchat is **pre-release** and under active development. The product shape,\npackaging, persistence "},{"id":"p40s2","text":"format, and ACP integration surface may change before a\nstable release. It is ready for local evalua"},{"id":"p40s3","text":"tion and development, not yet a\npromise of backwards compatibility."},{"id":"p41s1","text":"Issues and focused pull requests are welcome. For a useful bug report, include\nyour OS, Backchat bui"},{"id":"p41s2","text":"ld, agent/harness, project type, and the smallest reliable\nreproduction."},{"id":"p42s1","text":"## Learn more"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"- Agent Client Protocol\n- ACP session and subagent model\n- Codex / ChatGPT plugin compatibility\n- Fi"},{"id":"p43s2","text":"le-first storage RFC\n- Release and signing guide"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}

